# rule.always.entool-the-skills-you-touch

**when you use a skill and a brain still does part of the job, that leftover is a defect in the TOOL, not a duty of the caller.** name it; upsert the skill one rung closer to one deterministic call.

the WATCH half; `rule.always.externalize.tactics.into_skills` says write the skill.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you call a skill, then run a command to finish what it began | fold it inside |
| you read its output to decide the next call | candidate branch inside the tool |
| you call the same two skills in order, twice | one call |
| you read its instructions to know what to run | rung 2; ask what 🔩 looks like |
| a skill fails and you work around it by hand | 🔴 strongest signal; never leave unnamed |

test: 1. *what did I still figure out myself after one call?* naught → rung 4; else each step is an unclimbed rung (name the WORK, not turn count). 2. *judgment or step?* judgment (ambiguous case, intent, tradeoff) → stays with the brain, never fake determinism · a step, same every time → owed a tool.

act: small → do now · real work → seed or `.dream/` catch · judgment → document *"stays with the brain, because X"*. another repo's skill is re-seeded there.

blocker: a manual workaround for a broken skill, unrecorded · a tool that asserts determinism over genuine judgment.
